    "answer": {
        "text": "§\nAdverse Effects - Related to kidney (4) : Amphotericin B\n\n(1) Type I renal tubular acidosis\n\n(2) ⇒ Hypokalemia\n\n(3) & ⇒ Mg2+ wasting\n\n(4) ↓ EPO ⇒ Anemia\n\n(Type I RTA ⇒ More (-) luminal voltage ⇒ ↓ Driving force for Mg2+ reabsorption || ↑ Driving force for K+ secretion)\n\n[Image: 1ca3ba290673c904d1797fc2aeb25eddcd6f7c7665ff17db3a2b66e3c2494204]\n\n[Image: df871e4a6938c507055027977998a805eba59d6d4448d81deef556188671647b]\n\n[Image: 1107122d3d488744f7123c84b8432729d0bb55bfc3bb0ee856e50a799d3d8812]\n\n[Image: f2403230a6bcdb5975ac0bc7f59c1a362f06cd4f352aa3a23783a407cb61943d]\n\n5.1 - Amphotericin, flucytosine\n[Image: 1b5ef9e80679b88c53a62ff8080f4e3c7f53075f3c49a5f37b120709205d0f02]\n\n[Image: 9fea5bd77323260182de515cbffdde9b432b1f89133f3e2604ac45c707e00d63]\n\n[Image: fb48c171e859420e532b213516a0ea4e3c6c3f280d6874edde07b7bcec252ce5]\n\n[Image: a67623382ecfd97911d2fef4eed826b01e0e668e098272c6a4ea38eded47718d]",
